chapters/stochastic_integral.tex:665:  \\uses{def:elemStochIntegral, def:IsSquareIntegrable, def:quadraticVariation, def:L2M}\nblueprint/src/chapters/filtration_martingale.tex:42:  A function $f : T \\to E$ is cadlag if it is right continuous and the limit $\\lim_{s \\uparrow t} f(s)$ exists for all $t \\in T$.\nblueprint/src/chapters/filtration_martingale.tex:1083:\\begin{theorem}\\label{thm:tendsto_limitProcess_of_cadlag}\nblueprint/src/chapters/filtration_martingale.tex:1086:Let $X$ be an uniformly integrable cadlag martingale with respect to the filtration $\\mathcal{F}$.\nblueprint/src/chapters/filtration_martingale.tex:1296:\\begin{lemma}[Stopped Submartingale]\\label{lem:Submartingale.stoppedProcess_of_cadlag}\nblueprint/src/chapters/filtration_martingale.tex:1298:  Let $X:\\mathbb{R}_+ \\to \\Omega \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be a cadlag submartingale and $\\tau$ a stopping time.\nblueprint/src/chapters/filtration_martingale.tex:1316:  \\uses{thm:doob_ineq, lem:Submartingale.stoppedProcess_of_cadlag}\nblueprint/src/chapters/filtration_martingale.tex:1343:  \\uses{lem:doob_ineq_stop, lem:Submartingale.stoppedProcess_of_cadlag}\nblueprint/src/chapters/elementary.tex:273:\\begin{lemma}\\label{lem:cadlag_elemStochIntegralBilin}\nblueprint/src/chapters/elementary.tex:275:For $V \\in \\mathcal{E}_{T, F}$, $X : T \\to \\Omega \\to E$ a càdlàg process and a continuous bilinear map $B: E \\times F \\to G$, the elementary stochastic integral $V \\bullet_B X$ is càdlàg.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:261:  A stochastic process $X$ is locally cadlag if and only if it is cadlag almost surely.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:296:  The class of cadlag processes is stable.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:326:  We say a stochastic process $(M_t)_{t \\in T}$ is a local martingale if it is locally a cadlag martingale in the sense of\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:327:  Definition~\\ref{def:locally}. That is, there exists a localizing sequence $(\\tau_n)_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ such that for all $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$, the process $M^{\\tau_n}\\mathbb{I}_{\\tau_n > 0}$ is a cadlag martingale.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:335:A stochastic process is a local submartingale if it is locally a cadlag submartingale in the sense of Definition~\\ref{def:locally}.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:336:That is, there exists a localizing sequence $(\\tau_n)_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ such that for all $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$, the process $M^{\\tau_n}\\mathbb{I}_{\\tau_n > 0}$ is a cadlag submartingale.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:344:Every cadlag martingale is a local martingale.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:357:The class of cadlag martingales is stable. That is, if $M$ is a cadlag martingale and $\\tau$ is a stopping time, then the stopped process cadlag $M^{\\tau}\\mathbb{I}_{\\tau > 0}$ is also a martingale.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:363:  Clearly, the stopped process $M^{\\tau}\\mathbb{I}_{\\tau > 0}$ is cadlag and it remains to show that it is a martingale.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:377:The class of cadlag submartingales is stable. That is, if $M$ is a cadlag submartingale and $\\tau$ is a stopping time, then the stopped process $M^{\\tau}\\mathbb{I}_{\\tau > 0}$ is also a cadlag submartingale.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:530:Every càdlàg martingale is of class DL.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:534:Let $X$ be càdlàg martingale. By Lemma~\\ref{lem:Martingale.submartingale_convex_comp}, $(|X_t|)_{t \\in T}$ is a nonnegative càdlàg submartingale, and the result follows from Lemma~\\ref{lem:Submartingale.classDL} along with Lemma~\\ref{lem:uniformIntegrableIffNorm}.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:695:Assume $T$ is a linear order endowed with a topology making it first countable and $E$ is a pseudo-metric space. If $X$ is a càdlàg process then it maps compact sets of $T$ to bounded sets.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:709:If $X$ is a real-valued càdlàg and adapted process, then the sequence $\\tau_n := \\inf \\{t | X_t \\ge n\\}$ is a localizing sequence.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:743:If $X$ is a càdlàg process of class DL, then it has locally integrable supremum.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:758:If a process is càdlàg and locally of class DL, then it has locally integrable supremum.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:773:If $X$ is a càdlàg process, then it is locally of class DL if and only if it has locally integrable supremum.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:788:A càdlàg process is locally of class D if and only if it is locally of class DL.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:804:A càdlàg process is locally of class D if and only if it has locally integrable supremum.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:816:Every cadlag submartingale for a right-continuous filtration has locally integrable supremum.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:840:Every cadlag submartingale is locally of class D.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:845:By Lemma~\\ref{lem:locally_classD_iff_locally_classDL}, it suffices to show that every cadlag submartingale is locally of class DL.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:879:A local martingale is a cadlag martingale if and only if it is of class DL.\nblueprint/src/chapters/local_martingales.tex:890:A nonnegative local submartingale is a cadlag submartingale if and only if it is of class DL.\nblueprint/src/chapters/doob_meyer.tex:724:Let $S : [0,T] \\to \\Omega \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be a cadlag submartingale of class D on $[0,T]$.\nblueprint/src/chapters/doob_meyer.tex:778:\\begin{lemma}\\label{lem:M_n_cadlag_mg}\nblueprint/src/chapters/doob_meyer.tex:780:The martingale on $[0, T]$ defined by $t \\mapsto \\mathbb{E}[M^n_{2^n}\\vert\\mathcal{F}_t]$ admits a modification which is a 