ady available. If it is not available, record the exact missing statement needed for `predictablePart_eq_of_normalized_decomposition` in the task result and leave that theorem unadded rather than adding a new `sorry`.\n\n   Preserve all existing declaration signatures, including `doob_meyer`, `martingalePart`, `predictablePart`, and the existing accessor lemmas. Run `lake env lean BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` and then `lake build`.\n\n## Deferred Queue\n\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/QuadraticVariation.lean` remains blocked at `IsLocalMartingale.isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm`: `Locally.isSquareIntegrable_submartingale_sq_norm` is proved, but the remaining theorem currently lacks the `SigmaFiniteFiltration P F` context and a local square-integrable localization refinement.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/QuadraticVariationBrownian.lean` has no current sorry and now contains `martingale_brownian_sq_sub_time`. Add `quadraticVariation_brownian` only after the normalized Doob-Meyer choice layer and predictable-part uniqueness/identification route are available.\n- The earlier Standard Borel objective remains deferred by the current user hint. Stay on the stochastic-integral/Brownian quadratic-variation route.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
.archon/logs/iter-005/plan.jsonl:12:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .archon/task_pending.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Index\n<!-- One line per file. Update line numbers when the file changes. -->\n\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/Auxiliary/StandardBorel.lean:15` — 2 sorries: `BorelSpace.sum`, `BorelSpace.sigma`.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/Choquet/CompactSystem.lean:59` — 5 sorries: finite-union representation and compact-system closure lemmas.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/CadlagModification.lean:46` — 1 sorry: `exists_modification_left_right_limit`.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean:30` — 1 sorry: local Doob-Meyer decomposition. Current Brownian route needs a normalized choice layer above this theorem: a `doob_meyer_normalized` helper, `predictablePart`/`martingalePart` choices backed by that normalized helper if feasible, and a bottom-zero accessor for the choice-based `predictablePart`.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/Komlos.lean:353` — 5 sorries: convergence chain from uniform convex tails through `komlos_ennreal`.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/LocalMartingale.lean:96` — 1 sorry: stability of càdlàg submartingales.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/OptionalSampling.lean:190` — 2 sorries: bounded optional-sampling inequalities.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/QuadraticVariation.lean:84` — 1 sorry: `IsLocalMartingale.isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm`; transport through local square-integrability is done, but the remaining localization route is blocked by missing `SigmaFiniteFiltration P 𝓕` and a local square-integrable refinement under the current theorem signature.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/QuadraticVariationBrownian.lean` — no current sorry. `ProbabilityTheory.martingale_brownian_sq_sub_time` is proved; the remaining downstream theorem `ProbabilityTheory.quadraticVariation_brownian` is blocked on normalized Doob-Meyer predictable-part identification for the choice-based `predictablePart`.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/SquareIntegrable.lean:66` — 3 sorries: scalar closure and martingale convergence.\n- [ ] `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/UniformIntegrable.lean:201` — 1 sorry: uniform integrability of bounded stopped submartingales.\n\n---\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
